{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f37e39d99b57bc5b37", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243791"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243731", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ca", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80be"], "question": {"text": "In $\\mathrm{SO}_2, \\mathrm{NO}_2^{-}$and $\\mathrm{N}_3^{-}$the hybridizations at the central atom are respectively :"}, "options": [{"id": "8bc787", "text": "$\\mathrm{sp}^2, \\mathrm{sp}^2$ and sp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436cb"}, {"id": "8f0cf6", "text": "$\\mathrm{sp}^2, \\mathrm{sp}$ and sp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436cc"}, {"id": "099ce6", "text": "$\\mathrm{sp}^2, \\mathrm{sp}^2$ and $\\mathrm{sp}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436cd"}, {"id": "b67f48", "text": "$\\mathrm{sp}, \\mathrm{sp}^2$ and sp", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436cf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b64"], "question": {"text": "In which of the following processes, the bond order has increased and paramagnetic character has changed to diamagnetic?"}, "options": [{"id": "a4d909", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d0"}, {"id": "4ca4f0", "text": "<math><mi>N</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d1"}, {"id": "b624b9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d2"}, {"id": "155fc3", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ab79db6fe44bfe0fe4b3bb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R.</p><p>Assertion A : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Te</mi></math> is more acidic than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>.</p><p>Reason R: Bond dissociation enthalpy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Te</mi></math> is lower than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>.<br/>In the light of the above statements. Choose the most appropriate from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c55302", "text": "Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d5"}, {"id": "bc5990", "text": " Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d6"}, {"id": "4021c7", "text": "A is false but R is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d7"}, {"id": "702b46", "text": "A is true but R is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436d9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b3f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which of the following are isostructural pairs?</p><p>A. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>B. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>TiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p>C. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math></p><p>D. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "db90e0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436da"}, {"id": "e7fad7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436db"}, {"id": "1622a4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436dc"}, {"id": "408888", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436dd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436de", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements.</p><p>Statement I : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> are weakly attracted by magnetic field and are magnetized in the same direction as magnetic field.</p><p>Statement II :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> are weakly magnetized in opposite direction to magnetic field.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer form the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6c0dd1", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436df"}, {"id": "875634", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e0"}, {"id": "e9fc77", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e1"}, {"id": "8b73c5", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b89067dbe2603c3e80ce"], "question": {"text": "The reaction in which the hybridisation of the underlined atom is affected is"}, "options": [{"id": "b50547", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>H</mtext><mtext>3</mtext></msub><munder><mtext>P</mtext><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><msub><mtext>O</mtext><mtext>2</mtext></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mtext>Disproportionation</mtext></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e4"}, {"id": "52f387", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>H</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><munder><mtext>S</mtext><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><msub><mtext>O</mtext><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>NaCl</mtext><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mtext>420&#160;K</mtext></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e5"}, {"id": "9f566f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mtext>N</mtext><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><msub><mtext>H</mtext><mtext>3</mtext></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mtext>H</mtext><mo>+</mo></msup></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e6"}, {"id": "c278b5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mtext>X</mtext><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><msub><mtext>eF</mtext><mtext>4</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>SbF</mtext><mtext>5</mtext></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["6162fb826ed13040ec84fbd4"], "question": {"text": "The linear combination of atomic orbitals to form molecular orbitals takes place only when the combining atomic orbitals</p><p>A. have the same energy &nbsp;B. have the minimum overlap &nbsp;C. have same symmetry about the molecular axis &nbsp;D. have different symmetry about the molecular axis</p><p>Choose the most appropriate from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "962265", "text": "A, B, C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436e9"}, {"id": "22eb4e", "text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ea"}, {"id": "5b0189", "text": "B, C, D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436eb"}, {"id": "1f6209", "text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ec"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ed", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa394"], "question": {"text": "The compound that has the largest&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>H</mi></math> bond angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "2d6fb2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ee"}, {"id": "699168", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ef"}, {"id": "ed66d1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f0"}, {"id": "04f2d3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["617aa9e9ef3fe65ad8e837eb"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :<br/>Statement (I) : A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> bonding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MO</mi></math> has lower electron density above and below the inter-nuclear axis.</p><p>Statement (II) : The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></math> antibonding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MO</mi></math> has a node between the nuclei.</p><p>In light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "498d8f", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f3"}, {"id": "08a932", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f4"}, {"id": "05f2e0", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f5"}, {"id": "4dacbb", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9947"], "question": {"text": "The intermolecular potential energy for the molecules<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> ,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> , <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> given below suggests that:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fff423fa9-a8af-4f27-ae0f-0124c7f2324d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 299px; height: 220px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "785ffb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> has the shortest bond length", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f8"}, {"id": "b3ad17", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> has the largest bond enthalpy", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436f9"}, {"id": "3c2d7a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is more electronegative than other atoms.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436fa"}, {"id": "a07e50", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> has the stiffest bond.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436fb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436fc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b3f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List I with List II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 300px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\">List I</p>\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\">(molecules/ions)</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\">List II</p>\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\">(No. of lone pairs of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math><br />\t\t\ton central atom)</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>IF</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>I.</td>\t\t\t<td>Three</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ICl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>II.</td>\t\t\t<td>One</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>III.</td>\t\t\t<td>Two</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>IV.</td>\t\t\t<td>Zero</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the <strong>correct</strong> answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1d8eea", "text": "A - II, B - III, C - IV, D - I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436fd"}, {"id": "288060", "text": "A - IV, B - III, C - II, D - I", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436fe"}, {"id": "8f2ac1", "text": "A - II, B - I, C - IV, D - III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d92436ff"}, {"id": "ab8892", "text": "A - IV, B - I, C - II, D - III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243700"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243701", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa028"], "question": {"text": "The potential energy curve for the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> molecule as a function of internuclear distance is:"}, "options": [{"id": "b81032", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F348a8ff7-f1cd-4fdc-808a-1ff17ad8a74b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 177px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243702"}, {"id": "27cda4", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7c9dfbfd-7335-425f-8d0e-489317c24bdb-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 249px; height: 174px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f252ee0e063d9243703"}, {"id": "a33711", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fd2ab7ee3-289b-4dfe-b079-4a9676f7fafa-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 177px;\" />", "isCorr